Module: include/Player/Player.h
- Namespace: Player
- class Player { public:
  - explicit Player(const Time::IClock& clock);
  - void set_current_media(const Media::MediaMetadata* media);
  - const Media::MediaMetadata* current_media() const;
  - PlaybackState state() const noexcept;
  - std::int64_t position_ms() const noexcept;
  - std::int64_t duration_ms() const noexcept;
  - bool play();
  - void pause() noexcept;
  - void stop() noexcept;
  - void seek(std::int64_t ms) noexcept;
  - void update_to_now() noexcept;
  - int set_volume(int v) noexcept;
  - int volume() const noexcept;
  - void mute(bool m) noexcept;
  - bool muted() const noexcept;
  - int effective_volume() const noexcept;
  private:
  - const Time::IClock& clock_;
  - PlaybackState state_;
  - const Media::MediaMetadata* current_media_;
  - std::int64_t position_ms_;
  - std::int64_t last_tick_ms_;
  - int volume_;
  - bool muted_;
}
Contract:
- Header must directly contain #include <cstdint> and include Time/IClock.h, Media/MediaMetadata.h, and Player/PlaybackState.h.
- state_ initially Stopped; position_ms_ initially 0; current_media_ initially nullptr; last_tick_ms_ initialized from clock_.now_ms(). volume_ default 100, muted_ default false.
- set_current_media sets pointer; resets position to 0 and sets state to Stopped; updates last_tick_ms_ to clock_.now_ms(). Caller owns lifetime of media; pointer may be nullptr to clear.
- current_media returns the pointer (may be nullptr).
- state returns current playback state.
- position_ms returns current position in ms; always in [0, duration]. If no media, duration is 0 and position is 0.
- duration_ms returns media duration or 0 if no media.
- play returns true if state becomes Playing (when media is set and either Stopped or Paused); returns false if no media; if already Playing, leaves state and returns true; updates last_tick_ms_ to clock_.now_ms() when entering Playing.
- pause sets state to Paused if it was Playing; no-op otherwise.
- stop sets state to Stopped and position to 0; updates last_tick_ms_ to clock_.now_ms().
- seek clamps ms to [0, duration]; sets position; if state is Playing and position becomes >= duration, clamps to duration and sets state to Paused (end-of-media); updates last_tick_ms_ to clock_.now_ms() when state is Playing; otherwise leaves last_tick_ms_ as-is.
- update_to_now when state is Playing and media set: calculates delta = clock_.now_ms() - last_tick_ms_ (if delta <= 0, only updates last_tick_ms_); adds delta to position, clamps to duration; when clamped at end, sets state to Paused; always sets last_tick_ms_ to current clock_.now_ms(). When not Playing or no media, does nothing but may refresh last_tick_ms_ only when transitioning to Playing elsewhere.
- set_volume clamps v to [0, 100], stores, and returns the clamped value.
- volume returns the stored unclamped volume value (clamped in setter).
- mute sets muted_ flag; muted returns flag.
- effective_volume returns 0 if muted, otherwise volume().
- All methods marked noexcept in signature must not throw. All std::int64_t types are spelled exactly and headers include <cstdint> directly.

Module: include/Runtime/App.h
- Namespace: Runtime
- class App { public:
  - App();
  - int run_demo();
}
Contract:
- run_demo constructs Time::ManualClock with a deterministic start, a Playlist::Playlist, creates Media::MediaMetadata (non-negative duration), adds/selects item 0, constructs Player::Player with ManualClock, sets current media, calls play, advances ManualClock by a known delta (e.g., 1000 ms), calls update_to_now, then pauses or stops. Returns 0. No streaming or interactive loops; deterministic behavior suitable for headless environments.

Allowed include direction and boundaries:
- include/Time/IClock.h is the lowest-level boundary; it may include only <cstdint> and standard library.
- ManualClock.h and MonotonicClock.h include IClock.h and <cstdint>.
- MediaMetadata.h stands alone and depends only on <string> and <cstdint>.
- Playlist.h depends on MediaMetadata.h.
- PlaybackState.h stands alone.
- Player.h depends on Time/IClock.h, Media/MediaMetadata.h, and Player/PlaybackState.h.
- Runtime/App.h depends on Time/ManualClock.h, Playlist/Playlist.h, Player/Player.h, and Media/MediaMetadata.h.

Non-negotiable compile protocol:
- Every header that names a signed 64-bit integer directly includes <cstdint> and spells std::int64_t; bare int64_t is forbidden.
- include/Time/IClock.h declares exactly virtual std::int64_t now_ms() const noexcept = 0; and derived clocks override exactly that signature with identical const and noexcept in both headers and sources.
- tests/test_main.cpp is a single self-contained program using only standard library and the declared headers; no third-party test frameworks.
- CMake defines a core library from non-Main sources, a demo executable src/Main.cpp linked to that library, and a test executable linked to that library; enable_testing() and add_test() are present.
- src/Main.cpp only returns Runtime::App().run_demo() and does not stream enums.","Shared Knowledge":"This repository is a headless, deterministic C++17 video player domain model. The reusable interfaces are under include/*.h and must be self-contained: every header includes its own needed standard headers explicitly. All time values in public APIs use std::int64_t and headers that name them directly include <cstdint>. The Player advances based on a Time::IClock; tests use Time::ManualClock for determinism. Runtime::App wires ManualClock, Playlist, Player, and MediaMetadata together for a small demo. CMake builds a core library from all src/*.cpp except src/Main.cpp; both the demo and the single test target link against this core library. tests/test_main.cpp includes only declared include/*.h headers; it never includes src/*.cpp files or external frameworks.","Execution Protocol":"Build with CMake and C++17. Run tests with: ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure. One protocol-level test file exists: tests/test_main.cpp. It includes headers only and links to the core library. The runtime entry is src/Main.cpp, which contains only a minimal int main() returning Runtime::App().run_demo(). No interactive or long-running loops; no network or OS-dependent behavior. The core library contains all implementation sources except src/Main.cpp.","Anything UNCLEAR":""}

